From: Boden Fuller <boden.fuller@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 6 Jul 2026 12:26:53 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?patch(tmux):=20atomic-snapshot=20+=20identity-v?=
 =?UTF-8?q?erified=20session=20teardown=20=E2=80=94=20fix=20PID-reuse=20ki?=
 =?UTF-8?q?ll=20massacre?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

KillSession/KillPane{,WithProcesses,Excluding} discovered kill targets via a
slow live pgrep walk (seconds under load), then looped kill -TERM by bare PID.
During a stop/drain wave the collapsing agent trees free PIDs that the kernel
recycles onto unrelated processes (Finder, Dock, tmux, editors, other panes)
inside the walk->kill window, so the kill landed on the innocent new owner. On
macOS the reparented-to-init (PPID==1) group-member step made every GUI app a
candidate (launchd parents them all). Observed twice on 2026-07-06 (07:03,
08:34): ~25 SIGTERMs in 5s took out the whole login session.

Fix: discoverKillTargets snapshots the process table ONCE (ps -axo
pid,ppid,pgid,lstart), builds the descendant tree + reparented set from that
atomic snapshot, and stamps each target with its start time; killVerified
re-checks the start time immediately before signaling, so a recycled PID (new
start time) is skipped. Same local-fork lineage as the getAllDescendants
cycle-guard. Unit-tested (blast-radius containment + cycle termination).
